 Spoiler Alert!

  The command used to create new scroll from a blank one should be a(pply).
And you have a chance to be able to write a not-yet-encountered scroll--
with the risk of wasting a blank scroll and charges of the magic marker.
However, you can always write scrolls you've named (not *identified*) before.
For example, you have named both of the $300 scrolls(genocide and charging),
but you don't know which one is which. Now you can write either of the two 
with no risk.
